# Scoped Trivy ignore for the PostgreSQL image ONLY (see deploy.mjs
# scanImages()). Does not apply to the API, API-Operations, or Web images —
# those are scanned with the full HIGH/CRITICAL gate and no ignore file.
#
# Known upstream issue: /usr/local/bin/gosu, the privilege-drop utility
# bundled by the official docker-library/postgres image, is built with an
# older Go toolchain (v1.24.6) whose stdlib carries these fixed-upstream
# HIGH/CRITICAL CVEs. gosu is a third-party tool packaged by the image
# maintainer — it is not PostgreSQL itself, not our application code, and
# not the base OS: both the Alpine and Debian package layers scan clean
# (0 vulnerabilities) in every tag tested below.
#
# Verified 2026-10-15 on the staging VPS — identical gosu binary and CVE
# set across every current official tag tested:
#   postgres:16-alpine   (Alpine 3.24.2)
#   postgres:17-alpine   (Alpine 3.24.2)
#   postgres:16-bookworm (Debian 12.15)
# No tag swap resolves this; it requires docker-library/postgres to rebuild
# gosu against a current Go release.
#
# Tracked blocker: re-evaluate when docker-library/postgres ships a gosu
# rebuild, or replace gosu via a custom PostgreSQL image. Do not widen this
# file to cover any CVE outside this exact gosu set without re-justifying.
